+  // Adding a `{...}:` function header happens to hide the problem because the
+  // walk stops at the function body, which is why it appears to come and go.
+  //
+  // There is no sound way to tell statically which leading components are module
+  // plumbing, so try successively shorter suffixes and keep the first scope that
+  // actually resolves. The unmodified path is tried first, so well-formed
+  // modules keep their exact current behaviour and cost exactly one round-trip.
+  for (size_t Dropped = 0;
+       Dropped <= Scope.size() && Dropped <= MaxDroppedPrefixes; ++Dropped) {
